{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And he settled in the mountain, and his two daughters with him.</b> The deed of Lot's daughters was a novel matter, and they were modest and ashamed to demand of their father — for a son of Noah is permitted in his daughter." "<b>And our Rabbis of blessed memory</b> said that they intended for the sake of Heaven, in order to settle the world, for they saw the great destruction in that generation and feared the loss of the human species; and since their mother had already perished in becoming a pillar of salt, and their father was alone without his mate, therefore they needed to do this deed with him in order to keep seed alive from him and that the species not be lost. And from this they said in their argument: ״ואיש אין בארץ וגו׳״ — and there is no man in the earth, etc. And because of this you will not find that Scripture mentioned in them any expression of harlotry throughout the entire passage, for their intention was for the sake of Heaven; and therefore the elder merited that from her emerged Ruth the Moabitess, who accepted upon herself 248 commandments by which Israel exceeds the sons of Noah. And the younger merited that from her emerged Naamah the Ammonitess, from whom emerged Rehoboam son of Solomon; and so it is found that both of them merited the kingdom of the house of David. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said concerning the matter of Ammon and Moab: ״עמון ומואב אל תצורם ואל תתגר בם״ — do not seek their peace nor their welfare — on account of two good shoots that I am destined to bring forth from them: these are Ruth the Moabitess and Naamah the Ammonitess. And this passage is one of the passages of the Torah that are read and translated; and this is their statement at the end of tractate Megillah: the deed of Lot and his two daughters is read and translated — that is obvious! What might you say, that we should be concerned on account of the honor of Abraham? It teaches us."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:46.141703491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}